index 0000000..175e0c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Logging: archive, audit, alert
+
+Observability is split into three lanes. Pick the lane by **who needs to see it
+and how fast**, not by severity alone.
+
+| Lane | Purpose | How | Where | Retention |
+| ---- | ------- | --- | ----- | --------- |
+| **Archive** | Routine application logs (debug → error) for debugging | `Log::info(...)`, `Log::error(...)` (default `stack` → `daily`) | `storage/logs/laravel-YYYY-MM-DD.log` | 14 days (`LOG_DAILY_DAYS`) |
+| **Audit** | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` | `storage/logs/audit-YYYY-MM-DD.log` | 90 days (`LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`) |
+| **Alert** | An incident a human must act on now | `(new \App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert)->send($title, $message, $context)` | Discord incoming webhook | Discord's |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. Did something change state, or was a sensitive action attempted, and we may
+   need to prove it later (membership role change, subscription transition,
+   login lockout)? → **Audit**. Log the actor, the subject and the before/after.
+2. Is it actionable in production *and* worth waking someone up (job exhausted
+   its retries, payment-gateway webhook failing, plan limit blocking an entity)?
+   → **Alert**, and also write the normal **Archive** entry with the details.
+3. Anything else (flow tracing, handled errors, debug output)? → **Archive**.
+
+An event can belong to more than one lane; they are independent calls.
+
+## Archive
+
+`logging.channels.daily` (driver `daily`, `storage/logs/laravel.log`, level
+`LOG_LEVEL`, 14 days). The default `stack` channel (`LOG_STACK`, default
+`daily`) writes to it. `phpunit.xml` pins `LOG_STACK=daily` so tests do not depend
+on a local `.env`.
+
+## Audit
+
+`logging.channels.audit` (driver `daily`, `storage/logs/audit.log`, minimum level
+`LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL`, default `info`, retention `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`, default `90`).
+Keep entries structured and free of secrets/PII beyond identifiers:
+
+```php
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'entity_id' => $entity->id,
+    'actor_id' => $actor->id,
+    'from' => 'trial',
+    'to' => 'active',
+]);
+```
+
+## Alert (Discord)
+
+`App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send(string $title, string $message, array $context = []): void`.
+
+- Webhook from `services.discord.webhook_url` (`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`). Empty or
+  unset → silent no-op, no HTTP request.
+- POSTs `{"content": "<title>\n<message>\nkey=value..."}` with a short timeout.
+  The text is truncated to 1800 characters (Discord's limit is 2000).
+- Context is redacted: keys matching `password`, `token`, `secret`,
+  `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey` or `webhook`, and any string
+  containing `Bearer <credential>`, become `[redacted]`; nested arrays are
+  redacted recursively and rendered as JSON.
+- Soft-fail: it never throws. A non-2xx response or a transport error writes an
+  `error` entry to the archive, with the webhook URL scrubbed (it embeds the
+  token).
+
+**Discord is not a log channel.** There is deliberately no `discord` entry in
+`config/logging.php`: alerting is an explicit call by code that decided the
+incident is worth paging for. Do not route `Log::` levels to it (that would page
+on noise and loop on its own failures).
+
+## Env keys
+
+| Key | Default | Meaning |
+| --- | ------- | ------- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels of the default `stack` |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention (days) |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Audit minimum level |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention (days) |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty | Ops alert webhook; keep it secret |
